This project is easy to set up once you have installed docker desktop which can be easily done with `winget install Docker.DockerDesktop`
And then install dbeaver with `winget install dbeaver.dbeaver`.

if you have those installed it is easy, just open the shared-resources/src folder using terminal.
and run `docker-compose up -d` to create a docker container for the project. This way we do not need
to manually install all kinds of packages every time.

Then navigate to the project root directory inside terminal and run `./gradlew :json-http-client:test` just to check that everything is working properly
then run `.\gradlew run --warning-mode all` to run the app conventionally.

You can access the db using dbeaver, open it up